<Defs>

	<ThingDef ParentName="CGF1_MWP_ATLauncher_T2">
		<defName>CGF1_MWP_Type56_RPG_</defName>
		<label>Type 56 RPG</label>
		<description>Caliber: 82mm PG-2. 1-round tube. Single-Shot.
		
The Type 56 rocket-propelled grenade launcher is a Chinese copy of the Soviet RPG-2. Type 56 RPGs were widely used by the North Vietnamese Army and associated forces during the Vietnam War, where it and its domestic Vietnamese copies (the B-40 and B-50) acted as their standard man-portable anti tank weapons. The Type 56 was superceded by the Type 69 (a copy of the RPG-7) in the late 1960s, and has generally become obsolete in the anti-tank role in the present; nevertheless, Chinese Type 56s still pop up in conflicts around the world to this day, even despite the sheer popularity of its younger RPG-7/Type 69 siblings.</description>
